        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2025",
        "question_text": "<p>Given that $x - 2$ is a factor of $f(x) = x^3 - 4x^2 + ax + 6$, find the value of $a$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>By the Factor Theorem, if $x - 2$ is a factor, then $f(2) = 0$.<br><br>Substitute $x = 2$ into $f(x)$: $2^3 - 4(2)^2 + a(2) + 6 = 0$.<br><br>$8 - 16 + 2a + 6 = 0 \\Rightarrow -2 + 2a = 0 \\Rightarrow 2a = 2 \\Rightarrow a = 1$.</p>",
